    },
    {
      "facts": [3],
      "point": "A video conferencing system is not VR because it shows a real environment through a screen and lacks sensory immersion."
    },
    {
      "facts": [4],
      "point": "A 3D movie experience is not VR because it lacks interaction: viewers only watch and cannot change content."
    }
  ],
  "text": "A system must have a virtual environment, sensory immersion, and interaction to be a VR system; missing any one characteristic makes it non-VR. Applying that test, computer-aided design, video conferencing, and 3D movie systems are classified as non-VR. Each fails for a different reason: computer-aided design lacks sensory immersion, video conferencing presents a real environment through a screen without sensory immersion, and 3D movies are non-interactive."
}

